  "_comment": "Dubai communities used to place a company on the map when it has no geocodable street address (PLAN.md obstacle 3, tier a). Matching runs over the lowercased company name + address + address2 + zip. Each alias is turned into a regex: runs of spaces become a flexible separator class and the whole alias is wrapped in word boundaries, so the alias 'al quoz' matches 'Al-Quoz', 'AL QUOZ' and 'Alquoz'. The LONGEST matching alias wins, so 'Dubai Investment Park' beats 'Jebel Ali' on a string containing both.",
  "_created": "2026-09-19",
  "_rules": {
    "match_order": "longest alias first, measured on the alias string",
    "boundaries": "word boundaries on both ends, so a short alias such as jlt cannot match inside a longer word",
    "never_alias": ["dubai", "uae", "emirates", "po box", "street", "road"],
    "coordinates": "NOT stored here. Centroids are fetched from Nominatim by scripts/geocode-communities.js and written to data/communities.json together with the OSM place id that produced them. No coordinate in this project is invented."
  },
